  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Prospectus Summary",
      "excerpt": "Prospectus Summary Overview of Our Business Source Agriventures is an early stage farmland-focused real asset and sustainable agriculture company that seeks to generate long-term value by combining high-quality agricultural real estate with regenerative farming, clean-energy development and strategic Agricultural Technology (\u201c AgTech \u201d) investments. Source Agriventures has a limited operating history: We currently own one farming property located in Illinois and plan to acquire more, as part of a broader operational strategy that will include a number of business verticals. Our business is built on the belief that farmland is a scarce, essential and increasingly valuable resource, and that the next generation of agricultural land ownership will be driven not only by crop production, but also by improved land stewardship, diversified revenue streams and the integration of modern technolog",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of Proceeds We estimate that the net proceeds to us from our issuance and sale in this offering, after deducting the underwriting discounts and commissions and estimated offering expenses payable by us, will be approximately $ , assuming a public offering price per share of $ . If the Underwriter\u2019s over -allotment option is exercised in full, we estimate that our net proceeds will be approximately $\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0. We intend to use the net proceeds from this offering, together with our existing resources, as follows: \u2022 % for the acquisition of farmland properties (see \u201c Business and Properties \u2014 Future Opportunities \u201d); \u2022 % for strategic investments in AgTech companies; \u2022 % for the progression and development of AI data centers on farmland properties we acquire; \u2022 % for our operating expenses for the next 12\u00a0months; \u2022 % for prospectus and listing -related expenses; and \u2022 % for other wor",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk Factors Investing in our Common Stock involves a high degree of risk. Before investing in our Common Stock, you should carefully consider the risks described below, as well as the other information in this prospectus, including our financial statements and the related notes. In addition, we may face additional risks and uncertainties not currently known to us, or which as of the date of this Registration Statement we might not consider significant, which may adversely affect our business. If any of the following risks occur, our business, financial condition and results of operations could be materially adversely affected. In such case, the trading price of our Common Stock could decline due to any of these risks or uncertainties, and you may lose part or all of your investment. Risks Related to Our Business We have not reached profitability and currently have negative operating cas",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "Dilution If you invest in the Common Stock offered in this offering, your interest will be diluted immediately to the extent of the difference between the public offering price per share of Common Stock and the adjusted net tangible book value per share of our Common Stock after this offering. As of June 30, 2026, our net tangible book value was approximately $4,393,597, or $0.2114 per share. Our net tangible book value per share is equal to total assets less deferred financing and listing cost and total liabilities, divided by the number of our outstanding shares of Common Stock as of June 30, 2026. As adjusted net tangible book value dilution per share represents the difference between the amount per share paid by the new investors who purchase Common Stock in this offering and the as adjusted net tangible book value per share immediately after completion of this offering. After giving",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "Dividend Policy We have never paid any cash dividends on our Common Stock and do not anticipate paying any cash dividends on our Common Stock in the foreseeable future. We intend to retain future earnings to fund ongoing operations and future capital requirements. Any future determination to pay cash dividends will be at the discretion of our board of directors and will be dependent upon financial condition, results of operations, capital requirements and such other factors as the board of directors deems relevant. Transfer Agent and Registrar The transfer agent and registrar for our Common Stock is Odyssey Transfer and Trust Company, located at 860 Blue Gentian Rd, Suite 320, Eagan, Minnesota 55121. The transfer agent\u2019s telephone number is (612)\u00a0482 -5100 . Anti-Takeover Effects of Nevada Law and Our Articles of Incorporation and Bylaws General. Certain provisions of our Articles of Inc",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
